# 7. Layer 3 — Network Layer

## Definition

The Network Layer is responsible for **logical addressing and routing**.

The main addressing system is the **IP address**.

## Functions

* Logical addressing
* Routing
* Packet forwarding
* Path selection
* Connecting different networks

## Main Protocols

* IPv4
* IPv6
* ICMP
* IPsec

## Devices

* Router
* Layer 3 Switch

## Example

Suppose:

```text
PC A
192.168.1.10

      ↓

Router

      ↓

192.168.2.20
PC B
```

The router determines how the packet should travel from one network to another.

## Data Unit

**Packet**

## Important Concepts

* IP address
* Subnet mask
* Default gateway
* Routing table
* CIDR
* Network ID
* Host ID

## Troubleshooting

Useful commands:

```cmd
ipconfig /all
```

Check:

* IP address
* Subnet mask
* Default gateway
* DNS server

Test connectivity:

```cmd
ping 192.168.1.1
```

Check route:

```cmd
tracert google.com
```

